hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16742","He said: Umar ibn Sad Abu Dawud al-Hafari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaida narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Tariq narrated to me, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Imran ibn Husayn, he said: A Bedouin informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I fear for Quraysh only themselves; I said: What is with them; he said: Miserly, coarse; and if your life is prolonged you will see them tempting people until you see people among them like sheep between two ponds, to this one once and to this one once."
